course: dictionary
lesson: 3706
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Fledgling is one of these words. Its first meaning is a young bird that has just grown its feathers and is learning to fly. «A fledgling is usually best left alone or put in a bush close by.»
explain: Its second meaning is a person or thing that is new and not yet experienced. «A fledgling club» is a club that has only just started. Ask yourself: is the sentence about a bird, or about something new? The clues around the word will tell you.
explain: Look at the words near the word. «The fledgling hopped on the grass while its parents watched from the tree» tells you the bird is young and still learning, and that its parents are close by. The clues point to the bird meaning, so that is the one that fits.
fact: A fledgling is a young bird that has just grown its feathers and is learning to fly.
fact: Fledgling can also mean a person or thing that is new and not yet experienced, such as «a fledgling business».
fact: Fledgling can be a noun (a fledgling, fledglings) or an adjective (fledgling).
fact: A fledgling on the ground usually has its parents nearby, and they still feed it.
fact: Leave a fledgling alone unless it is hurt or in danger, for example from a cat.
exercise: «Molly found a fledgling on the grass.» What is a fledgling? | A large old bird with grey wings | A nest made of mud | *A young bird that is learning to fly | A type of worm
exercise: «The fledgling business had only opened last month.» What does fledgling mean here? | *New and not yet experienced | Old and broken | A bird that cannot fly | Very big and famous
exercise: Why should you usually leave a fledgling on the ground alone? | Birds on the ground are always hurt | Nobody is allowed to touch a bird ever | *Its parents are usually close by and still feed it | It has no feathers at all
test: What does «a fledgling club» mean? | A club with very old members | A club that has closed | *A club that has only just started | A club for birds
test: When should you call a rescue for a fledgling? | *Only if it is hurt or in danger, for example from a cat | Only when it is sitting on a branch | Every time you see one on the ground | Whenever it makes a noise
exam: Which meaning of fledgling fits «a fledgling bird hopping on the lawn»? | A business that has closed | A club that has only just started | A person who is very old | *A young bird that is learning to fly
